From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emilwojcik93 <adminit@adar.pl>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:01:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] posture: add the touch virtual display size policy

Windows has no tablet-mode switch. It docks the touch keyboard instead of
floating it over the app based on the physical monitor size the display
reports in its EDID, and a virtual display that reports a desktop-sized
monitor (27 in) makes the keyboard float over a touch client's stream.

Add the pure policy that decides which physical size a streaming client's
virtual display should report (src/posture_size.*):

- parse the optional clientPosture / clientTouch launch hints and the paired
  client "touch device" flag into a hint set; unknown values discard the hints;
- classify the client (desktop, laptop, tablet, handheld, phone) and apply the
  per-client override (auto, desktop, tablet, handheld);
- derive one fixed touch diagonal (default 356 mm, valid 100..419 mm) and split
  it by the stream aspect ratio, never by the client's own screen, DPI or EDID;
- keep the EDID-rounded diagonal below 17.0 in for every aspect so the docked
  keyboard stays docked (observed limit on Windows 11 build 26300).

Nothing calls the policy yet, so this patch changes no behaviour. Unit tests
cover parsing, classes, overrides, size derivation and the EDID bound.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
